# migrationProxyKey Function

The full source of the function:

```go
func migrationProxyKey(vmi *v1.VirtualMachineInstance) string {
	if vmi.Status.MigrationTransport == v1.MigrationTransportUnix &&
		vmi.IsMigrationTarget() &&
		vmi.Status.MigrationState != nil &&
		vmi.Status.MigrationState.SourceState != nil &&
		vmi.Status.MigrationState.SourceState.VirtualMachineInstanceUID != nil {
		return string(*vmi.Status.MigrationState.SourceState.VirtualMachineInstanceUID)
	}
	return string(vmi.UID)
}
```

It returns the source VMI's UID for decentralized UNIX-transport migrations, and otherwise falls back to the VMI's own UID.

# Usage in updateStatus

The function's return value is stored in `vmiUID` and passed to look up the target listener ports:

```go
vmiUID := migrationProxyKey(vmi)
destSrcPortsMap := c.migrationProxy.GetTargetListenerPorts(vmiUID)
if len(destSrcPortsMap) == 0 {
    msg := "target migration listener is not up for this vmi, giving it time"
    ...
}
```

# Usage in handleTargetMigrationProxy

Here the key is used both for detecting isolation and for constructing proxy keys per port:

```go
vmiUID := migrationProxyKey(vmi)
...
for _, port := range migrationPortsRange {
    key := migrationproxy.ConstructProxyKey(vmiUID, port)
    destSocketFile := migrationproxy.SourceUnixFile(baseDir, key)
    migrationTargetSockets = append(migrationTargetSockets, destSocketFile)
}
err = c.migrationProxy.StartTargetListener(vmiUID, migrationTargetSockets)
```

# finalCleanup Label/Annotation Handling

Near the end of `finalCleanup`, the target node name label is always removed, while the migration target annotation is only removed when the migration did not fail:

```go
// Effectively removes the VMI from our VMI informer
delete(vmi.Labels, v1.MigrationTargetNodeNameLabel)
if !vmi.Status.MigrationState.Failed {
    delete(vmi.Annotations, v1.CreateMigrationTarget)
}
return c.updateVMI(vmi, oldSpec, oldStatus, oldLabels, false)
```

The comment describes this as `"Effectively removes the VMI from our VMI informer"`. In short, deleting the target node name label detaches the VMI from the target controller's informer, and the `CreateMigrationTarget` annotation is preserved on failure so the failed state can be handled correctly.

